# Intro
Two 29.7 Msun stars in a periodic box of molecular gas, with the ISRF transport on
(`ISRF_propagation: 1`) and the H2 line absorption of the transport on
(`ISRF_H2_line_absorption: 1`). A dense slab (density contrast 300 at a uniform H2 ratio)
shadows star A. Star B sits in clear gas on the other side of the slab. A reception slot
spans about 90 degrees, and two lights share a slot only where their directions fall in
the same slot. Where the two lights fall in different slots (the check verifies this and
voids the run otherwise), they do not interact: the field of the two-star run must equal
the sum of the fields of two runs with one star each. The check tests that, tests the
carried H2 column of each star against the straight ray through the slab, and tests the
column of the two-star run against the one-star columns.

Read the README of `ISRFH2StarLit` for the build, the radiation table, the parameters that
the run holds fixed and the exit classes.

# Run
```
./run.sh
leg=switch_off ./run.sh       # line absorption off: the check must stop on the missing line fields
leg=stale_key ./run.sh        # an old GeajayCooling:h2_transported_lw_rate_shielding on the command line has no effect
```
The main leg runs swift four times with one binary: star A alone, star B alone, star A
alone again, and both stars. Each run is kept in its own directory (`only_a`, `only_b`,
`only_a2`, `main`). A star keeps its particle ID in the one-star runs, because the ID seeds the
random frame of the emission pixels. `run.sh` reads the number of reception slots from
`config.h` next to the `swift` executable. `contrast` (default 300), `level`, `gas_density`,
`gas_mass`, `h2_ratio` and `n_threads` override the defaults.

# Checking
`checkH2Attenuation.py twosource` reads the first and last snapshot of the two-star run,
the last snapshots of the three one-star runs (`--only-a`, `--only-b`, `--repeat-a`, run
directories), `fixture.json`, the parameters, the logs and `--slots`. The reference is
snapshot 1, the first written after the first step. The check is void (exit class 4) if
the four runs differ in parameters or build, or if the light of the two stars shares a slot
at a particle that holds both.

It tests that:
- the own LW energies of the two-star run equal the sums of the one-star fields, within the
  round-off of a reordered float sum;
- the carried H2 column of each one-star run follows the straight ray from the star through
  the slab and the clear gas;
- where both stars are lit, the column of the two-star run is the mean of the one-star
  columns weighted by their dissociating energies. This needs
  `ISRF_packet_read_mean_time_Myr = 0` (the default).
